well 52 year old eric echavarria was  killed just down the street from where  he lived tonight as you can imagine  his family is still in shock they tell  me eric was heading home from picking up  food for his son when  this crash happened now these are photos  the family shared with me earlier today  eric's wife ann marie tells me he leaves  behind a son stepchildren and a grant  and grandchildren  he was a military veteran and a  custodian for nearly 20 years at ccsd  anne marie has a message for those who  may be going out tonight  don't drive under the influence and  don't speed  he's a great dad great husband  he's living back behind her  fourteen-year-old son  and four step kids and  six grandkids um great guy great  provider  i'm actually there's a loss of words  that hasn't really sunk in yet  i'm trying the best i can  i spoke to a man who lives at the home  where this crash happened he says fort  apache is a road  known to many in that area for speeders  he wants to see more enforcement in that  area to  slow people down now the family plans to  hold a vigil this sunday at 6 pm near  where this crash happened at furnace  gulch  and fort apache reporting live joe  mohler 8 news now
 

